<title>USA: Motorola launches sports pager on Internet.</title>
<headline>Motorola launches sports pager on Internet.</headline>
<dateline>BOYNTON BEACH, Fla. 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Motorola Inc said Tuesday its EMBARC subsidiary launched the interactive ESPNET TO GO sports pager on the Internet.</p>
<p>ESPNET allows Internet users to click on the pager to receive the latest sports scores and information from around the world.</p>
<p>ESPNET TO GO is a comprehensive sports information service providing portable game information and score updates every five minutes from ESPN, which provides sports programming on cable television.</p>
<p>ESPN is owned 80 percent by Walt Disney Co.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
